Subject: Dictated Cantor M2B Supplied Regular File Topology Projection Source

Description: Raw selected build input for a pure transform that consumes one successful output-only supplied-content stable binding and one strict caller placement plan, applies exact correlation and component gates, and preserves a complete structurally valid M2A regular-file topology projection beside all lower-level supplied evidence. This source grants no physical path, Git, traversal, ordinal-assignment, stream-completeness, filesystem, receipt, or admission authority.

& [SourceIdentity] is preserved build input
  + [source_uuid] is a9f5b615-ab49-4e03-8320-749a3e09be04
  + [source_snapshot_uuid] is 6d302fd4-5fd5-44d5-99e0-fb7d65959ec2
  + [conversation_uuid] is cab190f5-eda0-44e0-81a5-51f9605e0baa
  + [selected_by_review_uuid] is 3829d2f6-af7c-4f24-96c6-b7d4500f409e
  + [working_profile] is cantor-windows-supplied-regular-file-topology-projection/0.1
  + [prerequisite_content_signature_uuid] is 44749466-30d8-44e9-85b8-e51f1bafea33
  + [prerequisite_topology_forms_signature_uuid] is 0e2cfacb-8659-41c2-b804-0eb1b49ff5b2
  + [authority_state] is unprocessed_source

& [Purpose] completes one supplied structural regular-file form without inflating provenance
  + start from the output-only WindowsSuppliedContentStableBinding created by the proven content-digest path
  + accept only the still-missing placement fields through a distinct strict caller plan
  + correlate the plan to the binding by exact caller-owned entry-reference syntax
  + require the plan path's final component to equal the previously policy-admitted component exactly
  + construct one complete TopologyEntryObservation using only mapped binding facts and copied plan facts
  + run current M2A structural validation on the constructed form
  + preserve the complete plan, complete content binding, and complete projected form together
  - never: accept a caller-asserted digest, a bare stable pair, or a bare projection seed as sufficient evidence
  - never: describe a successful output as physically observed, scanner-produced, Git-reconciled, traversed, admitted, or safe to mutate

& [InputSeparation] keeps two evidence grades visible
  + [binding] is a successful non-Deserialize private-field WindowsSuppliedContentStableBinding value passed by value
  + [plan] is strict serializable caller syntax for placement only
  + [derived_binding_facts] are regular kind, attributes, strong identity, link count, stream facts, length, and SHA-256 derived along the signed pure prerequisite path
  + [declared_plan_facts] are projection identity, entry-reference identity, relative path, mode class, and observation ordinal
  + [join_facts] are exact entry-reference equality and exact final-component equality
  - never: merge these grades into one unlabeled input bag

& [PlanShape] is strict and bounded
  + [profile] is exactly cantor-windows-supplied-regular-file-topology-projection/0.1
  + [projection_identity] is a nonzero caller-owned u64 local to the projection attempt
  + [entry_reference_identity] is a nonzero caller-owned u64 expected to match the supplied-content binding
  + [relative_path] is one caller-supplied String intended as an M2A descendant path
  + [mode_class] is one TopologyModeClass value and must be regular_non_executable or regular_executable
  + [observation_ordinal] is a nonzero caller-owned u64
  = must: serde JSON denies unknown fields, omissions, wrong types, and unknown enum values
  = must: any plan decoder rejects encoded input larger than 262144 bytes before JSON decoding
  - never: include kind, attributes, identity, links, streams, length, digest, physical path handles, clocks, or booleans claiming provenance in the plan

& [ProfileGate] is exact
  + unknown profile rejects before inspecting or projecting the binding
  + profile comparison is exact Unicode String equality
  + no aliases, prefixes, case folding, or version fallback exist

& [IdentityGates] are caller syntax only
  + projection_identity must be nonzero
  + entry_reference_identity must be nonzero
  + plan entry_reference_identity must exactly equal binding content-observation entry_reference_identity
  + plan entry_reference_identity must therefore retain the binding's already-proven equality with the stable pair
  + projection_identity and entry_reference_identity may be equal because they are different typed roles expressed in one scalar namespace; equality grants no additional meaning
  - never: treat either identity as a file handle, memory address, global key, database primary key, cryptographic identity, physical object identity, or persistent scanner identity

& [PathGate] reuses M2A syntax and adds exact component correlation
  + construct the candidate TopologyEntryObservation with Some(relative_path)
  + use current ValidateTopologyForm to enforce nonempty, nonrooted, slash-normalized, bounded descendant syntax
  + reject leading slash, trailing slash, backslash, colon, NUL, empty segment, dot segment, dot-dot segment, or case-insensitive .git segment through current M2A validation
  + extract the final slash-delimited component only after the path is structurally valid
  + require exact String equality between that final component and binding.stable_pair.pre_read.policy_decision.component
  + stability has already proved that pre-read and post-read policy decisions are exactly equal
  - never: case fold, Unicode normalize, trim, resolve, canonicalize, join to a root, inspect a filesystem, or interpret equality as physical path binding

& [ModeGate] is structural and honest
  + accept TopologyModeClass::RegularNonExecutable
  + accept TopologyModeClass::RegularExecutable
  + reject TopologyModeClass::Directory
  + preserve the exact accepted enum in both the plan and projected form
  + describe the accepted value as caller-declared mode class only
  - never: claim the mode came from Git, an index, a tree object, a work-tree query, a filesystem executable bit, a filename extension, or Windows attributes
  - never: infer executable mode from the supplied Windows attribute set

& [OrdinalGate] is structural and honest
  + require observation_ordinal nonzero
  + preserve it exactly in the plan and projected form
  + describe it as caller-declared ordering syntax only
  - never: prove monotonicity, uniqueness, predecessor relation, traversal position, complete inventory order, or scanner ownership from one ordinal

& [BindingConsumption] protects the lower-level construction path
  + take WindowsSuppliedContentStableBinding by value
  + do not accept serialized binding JSON because the binding intentionally has no Deserialize implementation
  + do not accept WindowsSuppliedContentDigestObservation, WindowsSuppliedEntryStablePair, or WindowsTopologyEntryProjectionSeed independently
  + do not reconstruct or clone the binding from public lower-level records
  + preserve the consumed complete binding in a successful output
  + on any fault, release no binding, plan, projection, or partial successful wrapper
  - never: add a public constructor, Default, Deserialize, or mutable field surface to the binding

& [ProjectionMapping] is exact and closed
  + call topology_projection_seed on binding.stable_pair.pre_read
  + require the seed kind is TopologyEntryKind::RegularFile
  + set relative_path to Some(plan.relative_path clone)
  + set kind to the exact seed kind
  + set mode_class to the exact accepted plan mode class
  + set attributes to the exact seed attributes
  + set identity to the exact cloned seed StrongFileIdentity
  + set number_of_links to the exact seed link count
  + set streams to the exact seed TopologyStreamFact collection and order
  + set length to the exact seed length
  + set content_sha256 to Some(binding.content_observation.derived_sha256 clone)
  + set observation_ordinal to the exact plan ordinal
  - never: substitute a default, normalize a mapped value, discard a stream, invent a field, or recompute the digest from text

& [TopologyValidation] is mandatory and current
  + invoke ValidateTopologyForm::validate on the newly constructed TopologyEntryObservation before success
  + preserve the exact TopologyFormFault as a nested boxed fault when validation rejects
  + label the wrapper fault code topology_form exactly when the nested fault is present
  + release no projected observation when validation rejects
  + current M2A authority remains the owner of canonical path, stream, digest, kind, mode, link, identity, and ordinal structural rules
  - never: duplicate a weaker local approximation of the M2A validator and skip the authority implementation
  - never: interpret M2A validation success as scanner admission

& [OutputShape] preserves lineage and prevents accidental downgrade
  + [profile] is exactly cantor-windows-supplied-regular-file-topology-projection/0.1
  + [plan] is the complete validated placement plan
  + [content_binding] is the complete consumed WindowsSuppliedContentStableBinding
  + [topology_observation] is the complete validated TopologyEntryObservation
  + all output fields are private
  + immutable getters expose each complete nested value by reference
  + Serialize is permitted for inspection and evidence
  + Deserialize, Default, public constructors, public fields, and mutable getters are absent
  - never: implement From or Into that returns a bare TopologyEntryObservation and silently loses the provenance wrapper
  - never: return only a boolean, digest, path, ordinal, or flattened record

& [FaultShape] is closed and bounded
  + [codes] are json, profile, projection_identity, entry_reference_identity, entry_reference, path, component, mode, ordinal, kind, topology_form, and resource
  + [nested_topology_fault] is present exactly for topology_form and absent for every other code
  + [field] is deterministic and no longer than 64 Unicode scalar values
  + [message] is deterministic and no longer than 256 Unicode scalar values
  + Display and Error expose only bounded field and message text
  + malformed encoded JSON text or parser diagnostics are bounded before release
  - never: include the complete encoded plan, content bytes, hash state, complete path beyond the bounded message policy, or serialized binding in diagnostics

& [EvaluationOrder] is deterministic
  + [step_1] enforce encoded-plan byte cap before JSON decode when using the decoder
  + [step_2] strict-decode the complete plan
  + [step_3] require exact profile
  + [step_4] require nonzero projection identity
  + [step_5] require nonzero plan entry-reference identity
  + [step_6] require regular mode class
  + [step_7] require nonzero observation ordinal
  + [step_8] require plan and binding entry-reference equality
  + [step_9] create the exact mapped candidate topology form
  + [step_10] run current M2A validation, including canonical descendant path syntax
  + [step_11] require exact final-component and stable policy-component equality
  + [step_12] release one output-only wrapper
  = must: every rejection has one stable fault code and deterministic field

& [SemanticStrength] keeps every claim at its evidence grade
  + [supplied] means presented by the caller or produced by an earlier pure supplied-value transform
  + [derived_digest] means SHA-256 of exact chunks accepted by the prerequisite accumulator
  + [stable_binding] means exact structural join to two equal supplied metadata assemblies
  + [relative_path] means canonical descendant-path syntax supplied in the plan
  + [mode_class] means a regular mode enum supplied in the plan
  + [observation_ordinal] means a positive scalar supplied in the plan
  + [component_correlated] means exact text equality between final path component and policy component
  + [topology_projection] means a structurally valid M2A value nested with its source evidence
  - never: claim physical origin, existence, root membership, same-object correspondence, completeness, freshness, actual time order, Git truth, traversal truth, trust, authenticity, atomic snapshot, immutability, admission, or mutation safety

& [DataDesignIntent] is explicit
  + [conceptual_model] combine a derived supplied content-and-stability evidence node with a declared placement node through exact structural relations
  + [logical_model] strict plan plus output-only binding to gates to M2A candidate to validation to output-only wrapper
  + [physical_model] safe deterministic in-memory Rust using serde and existing crate types only
  + [source_data] placement plan and content binding
  + [derived_data] one M2A topology observation and wrapper profile
  + [identity_namespace] caller-owned and invocation-local
  + [persistence] is absent
  + [state] is absent beyond stack-owned function inputs

& [ResourceBoundary] is bounded
  + encoded plan is capped at 262144 bytes before decode
  + relative path is bounded by current M2A validation at 32768 UTF-8 bytes
  + fault fields are capped at 64 Unicode scalar values
  + fault messages are capped at 256 Unicode scalar values
  + stream count and stream text are inherited from already successful lower-level values and rechecked by M2A validation
  + projection allocates only the bounded plan, cloned bounded seed facts, digest text, and output wrapper
  - never: walk, recurse, retain content chunks, read a file, enumerate a directory, or grow an unbounded collection

& [ImplementationBoundary] is zero effect
  + one new module is crates/cantor_ecosystem/src/windows_supplied_regular_file_topology_projection.rs
  + one exact library module export is allowed
  + module unit tests, one independent static test, evidence rehash, and workspace regression tests are allowed
  + production imports are std formatting, serde, topology forms, windows supplied entry observation seed support, and windows supplied content digest binding support
  + Cargo dependency and lockfile deltas are zero
  + unsafe is absent
  - never: import filesystem, path-resolution, Windows API, windows-sys, handle, pointer, buffer, process, command, environment, clock, random, network, persistence, database, model, Git, receipt, admission, mutation, seal, cleanup, review execution, or promotion facilities

& [TestIntent] is requirement centered
  + strict valid plan and bounded JSON decode succeed
  + unknown, omitted, malformed, and oversized plan inputs fail closed
  + zero projection identity, zero entry-reference identity, directory mode, and zero ordinal each fault exactly
  + entry-reference mismatch faults before projection
  + malformed relative path faults through nested M2A topology-form preservation
  + final-component mismatch faults exactly after structural path validity
  + both regular_non_executable and regular_executable modes project exactly
  + valid projection preserves plan, complete binding, exact seed facts, exact derived digest, and complete M2A form
  + a multi-segment path whose final component matches succeeds
  + serialization exposes inspectable lineage while compile/static assertions deny Deserialize, public-field construction, From, Into, effects, unsafe, and forbidden imports
  + debug and overflow-checked release focused tests pass
  + full workspace debug and overflow-checked release tests pass with only the already governed physical ignore
  + format, warnings-denied lint, release build, warnings-denied docs, audit, evidence rehash, and recursive artifact-reference checks pass

& [ProposedRequirementSet] is M2B-SRTP-001 through M2B-SRTP-014
  + [M2B-SRTP-001] strict bounded placement plan and exact profile
  + [M2B-SRTP-002] nonzero projection and entry-reference syntax
  + [M2B-SRTP-003] output-only content binding consumed as the sole lower-level evidence input
  + [M2B-SRTP-004] exact plan-to-binding entry-reference equality
  + [M2B-SRTP-005] canonical descendant relative-path validation through current M2A authority
  + [M2B-SRTP-006] exact final-component to stable policy-component equality
  + [M2B-SRTP-007] closed regular mode classes with caller-declared meaning
  + [M2B-SRTP-008] nonzero caller-declared ordinal with no traversal claim
  + [M2B-SRTP-009] exact seed, digest, and placement mapping without invention
  + [M2B-SRTP-010] mandatory current M2A topology-form validation and nested fault preservation
  + [M2B-SRTP-011] output-only lineage-preserving wrapper
  + [M2B-SRTP-012] closed bounded atomic fault behavior
  + [M2B-SRTP-013] explicit supplied structural projection semantics and physical nonclaims
  + [M2B-SRTP-014] zero-effect implementation and complete focused, global, evidence, quality, rollback, and downstream stop-gate proof

& [RollbackIntent] is deletion before downstream adoption
  + before any separately authorized consumer exists, rollback removes the new module export, tests, evidence manifest, solution, proof, review, and status entries
  + source, SJS, registry, narrative, and fault history remain as historical records
  + no schema migration, persisted value rewrite, filesystem repair, or effect cleanup is required

& [DownstreamStopGate] remains strict
  + a later directory projection must be separately sourced because this profile is regular-file only
  + a later inventory reconciler must consume provenance-preserving wrappers rather than arbitrary bare entries
  + a physical producer must separately prove owned-handle origin, initialized buffers, query completion, actual pre-content-post order, and content acquisition
  + a Git reconciler must separately prove exact path and executable-mode truth
  + traversal must separately own canonical ordering and ordinal assignment
  + receipt issuance must separately prove complete repeated inventory, freshness, resource accounting, and predecessor binding
  - never: infer any later authority from successful tests of this pure projection

& [SourceBoundary] is preservation only
  + this document is raw selected build input
  + SJS must delineate, explode, semantically refine, constraint-check, prune, growth-seed, data-design, fold, justify, plan, register, and sign it before implementation
  + canonical artifacts must remain separate from this file
  + the eventual signature must bind this exact source snapshot, current prerequisite signatures, all processed artifacts, and exact implementation boundary
  - never: treat source preservation as canonical, implementation, execution, or physical authority
